      "writtenOn": "2022-04-08T08:30:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this commit, bpf_skb_pull_data(skb, ..) may be called in sch_handle_ingress (bpf ingress). \nIs it possible to break that the skb in \"another_round\" trip (if any)? ex: deliver_skb try to clone modified skb for ptype_all in another_round trip\n\nhttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v5.10.94/source/net/core/dev.c#L5144\n\nstatic int __netif_receive_skb_core(struct sk_buff **pskb, bool pfmemalloc,\n\t\t\t\t    struct packet_type **ppt_prev)\nanother_round:\n..\n    list_for_each_entry_rcu(ptype, \u0026ptype_all, list) {\n        if (pt_prev)\n            ret \u003d deliver_skb(skb, pt_prev, orig_dev);\n\n    if (static_branch_unlikely(\u0026ingress_needed_key)) {\n..\n        skb \u003d sch_handle_ingress(skb, \u0026pt_prev, \u0026ret, orig_dev,\n        if (another)\n            goto another_round; // --\u003e starts a new trip with modified skb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 60,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "4b1e0f8bcfcbe4027ad4ce53b4a806d19f8c7aa2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47fd7a53_24fcc582",
        "filename": "bpf_progs/clatd.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 60,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-11T17:30:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "bpf_skb_pull_data(skb, len) just calls:\n  return bpf_try_make_writable(skb, len ? : skb_headlen(skb));\n\nwhich in turn just becomes:\n  int err \u003d __bpf_try_make_writable(skb, write_len);\n  bpf_compute_data_pointers(skb);\n  return err;\n\nwhere __bpf_try_make_writable() is just:\n  skb_ensure_writable(skb, write_len);\n\nthis in turn becomes:\n  if (!pskb_may_pull(skb, write_len)) return -ENOMEM;\n  if (!skb_cloned(skb) || skb_clone_writable(skb, write_len)) return 0;\n  return pskb_expand_head(skb, 0, 0, GFP_ATOMIC);\n\nWhich basically makes sure some number of bytes are in the linear portion of the packet header and breaks copy-on-write semantics (unclone)",
      "parentUuid": "8d9b70da_0d42e2a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 60,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "4b1e0f8bcfcbe4027ad4ce53b4a806d19f8c7aa2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50c61531_be0245fe",
        "filename": "bpf_progs/clatd.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 60,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-11T17:33:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ie. calling this twice on the same skb is fine, the first time we\u0027ll linearize a portion of the header of the packet and break copy-on-write semantics, the next time it\u0027ll be a no-op (unless it was cloned again in the mean time, in which case we\u0027ll break cow semantics again).",
      "parentUuid": "47fd7a53_24fcc582",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 60,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "4b1e0f8bcfcbe4027ad4ce53b4a806d19f8c7aa2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
